   "body": "## Goal\nReport, do not fix. Independently review the new public-development C1 challenge package from #597 against pinned source evidence and existing grading authority. Expected gain: a source-derived initial adjudication ledger, a comparison retaining disagreements, and separate Standards/Spec verdicts that tell the next shaper whether this procedure and its authored expectations are usable or need specific corrections. This is a new-scope agent usability/semantic review, not human adjudication, a new general scorer, or a repeat of closed #594 incorporation review. No session can run LabVIEW; claim no native validity, behavior, build, dependency resolution or save-version preservation.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] FIRST, before opening any later-read expectation-bearing file or running any checker, independently derive and save .session/artifacts/c1-challenges-cold-0126.json from the allowed-first authority, raw cases and original/conditional source bytes. Include observed HEAD/tree, package/source pins, identity/provider/model/continuity and prior-exposure declarations, exact raw-answer hashes, atomic assertion byte spans, subject/property/value/conditions, required-ID/slot mappings, missing slots, extras, duplicates, contradictions, citation resolution/support, separate correctness/grounding and whole-answer judgments with source rationales. Save and hash the initial ledger and record completion before later reads. If early exposure occurs, preserve it explicitly and refuse a cold-independence claim; never silently restart or erase it.\n- [ ] Verify the package and protected-source identities before interpretation using the permitted pin-only reads. The report of #597 pins c1-challenges-0125-verification.json to 7784 bytes/SHA256 ce8642fc2c2b23e826cb24786fbc06c9a3319c978f30e4fdb1c7389a01540fbc; cases SHA256 73dfd06532782777d5cc7390fef290c5ef079730ed41ac9bd5786956d2b0a710; expectations SHA256 5b3761ae2b8e351038b9b2ace8b5a684940009b55e1fbee9d0907ff642864071.